24m4|a|Offensive to the sight; contrary to beauty; being of disagreeable or loathsome aspect; unsightly; repulsive; deformed. ; Ill-natured; crossgrained; quarrelsome; as, an ugly temper; to feel ugly. ; Unpleasant; disagreeable; likely to cause trouble or loss; as, an ugly rumor; an ugly customer.	e:1oar,51,5;2753,31,3~1oar,51,5;2753,31,3
